      "file": "upstream-ui/docker-entrypoint.sh",
      "root_cause": "nginx.conf includes /etc/nginx/conf.d/api-proxy.inc* as a glob (silently matches nothing if absent). docker-entrypoint.sh only writes api-proxy.inc when UPSTREAM_API_PROXY_URL is set. When that env var is missing on the deployed pod, /api/v1/* requests fall through to the catch-all `location /` (try_files $uri $uri/ /index.html) and nginx returns the SPA shell (200 OK, index.html) instead of proxying to the backend. Confirmed in nginx access logs: every /api/v1/* and SPA route request returned exactly '200 502' (502 bytes = index.html size), while /tapis-proxy/v3/pods (always generated, unconditional) returned real proxied payloads. The generated OpenAPI TS client then fails to parse the HTML body as JSON and surfaces a generic error.",
